warrant:
STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIP WARRANT — PULSE INTELLIGENCE LABS, INC.

Issued to EDNA, Inc.

THIS STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIP WARRANT (this “Warrant”) is dated September 23, 2026 and issued only upon satisfaction of its closing conditions by Pulse Intelligence Labs, Inc., a Delaware corporation (the “Company”), to EDNA, Inc. (the “Holder”), in connection with:

the Strategic Partnership and Integration Agreement between the Parties dated September 11, 2026 (the “Partnership Agreement”);

the Reciprocal Strategic Equity Side Letter dated September 23, 2026 (the “Side Letter”); and

the reciprocal corporate authorizations adopted by the Parties.

The Company and Holder intend this Warrant to reflect a reciprocal company-to-company strategic equity arrangement and not to alter the commercial, operational, Intellectual Property, data, clinical, regulatory, or liability allocations established in the Partnership Agreement.

1. WARRANT GRANT

Subject to the terms and conditions of this Warrant, the Company grants to the Holder the right to purchase up to 200,000 shares of the Company’s common stock (the “Warrant Shares”). This is the purchase-right component only; the Holder’s separate 200,000-share Strategic Share Award is governed by the PIL Strategic Vesting Share Agreement dated September 23, 2026 and the Side Letter and requires no cash purchase.

Number of Warrant Shares: 200,000 maximum, subject only to Section 17 proportionate adjustments.

The Warrant covers a fixed maximum of 200,000 common shares and is not calculated as a percentage of Fully Diluted Capitalization. The separate Share Award does not reduce this cap, and exercise of this Warrant does not satisfy the Share Award. Ordinary financing dilution or conversion of existing instruments does not increase this Warrant’s share count.

Before this Warrant becomes effective, the Company shall document sufficient authorized and uncommitted shares for both components and disclose its capitalization, including the treatment, as applicable, of:

outstanding common stock;

preferred stock on an as-converted basis;

outstanding options;

outstanding warrants;

SAFEs or similar instruments;

convertible notes or other convertible securities;

reserved but unissued equity incentive plan shares; and

other outstanding rights to acquire Company equity.

The 200,000-share Warrant cap, exercise price, and sufficient share reservation shall be approved under applicable corporate requirements before this Warrant becomes effective. Capitalization disclosure shall not recalculate the fixed share count.

2. RECIPROCAL NATURE OF WARRANT

PIL’s Share Award and Warrant shall have no force or effect until EDNA delivers its valid reciprocal Share Award and separate Warrant, required approvals, and capitalization certificate at coordinated closing. EDNA’s reciprocal Share Award must represent 2.0% of EDNA’s fully diluted capitalization at that closing. If the fixed 200,000 shares do not meet that condition, both Parties must sign an amendment and obtain all required corporate approvals before closing; there is no automatic change to either share count. The condition is an initial closing test, not a continuing anti-dilution right. The PIL Share Award’s Section 6 governs reciprocal delivery and later breach remedies.

This Warrant is issued as part of a reciprocal strategic equity arrangement between the Company and Holder.

The Company’s issuance of this Warrant is conditioned upon the Holder:

obtaining all required corporate approvals for its corresponding strategic equity issuance to the Company;

executing the Side Letter;

granting to the Company a reciprocal Strategic Share Award for 200,000 common shares and issuing a separate Warrant to purchase up to 200,000 additional common shares, each with the matching four-year vesting schedule and one-year cliff; and

executing definitive documentation materially consistent with the reciprocal economic and legal principles set forth in the Side Letter.

The Parties intend the reciprocal warrants or equity instruments to be executed and issued contemporaneously or as nearly contemporaneously as reasonably practicable.

Neither Party shall be required to issue its reciprocal strategic equity instrument materially earlier than the other Party unless both Parties expressly agree otherwise in writing.

Procedural differences required by applicable law or governing documents may be used, but both reciprocal components shall retain their fixed common-share counts, matching vesting schedules, and substantive protections. Any change of security class or fixed share count requires both Parties’ written agreement and all required corporate approvals, except for expressly permitted proportionate corporate adjustments. Equal share counts do not represent a promise of equal ownership percentages or equal dollar values.

3. STRATEGIC COMMERCIAL PURPOSE; SECURITIES TREATMENT

This Warrant is being issued in connection with the Parties’ strategic commercial relationship, which may include:

Joint Services commercialization;

product and technical integration;

pilot collaboration;

Clinical Handoff infrastructure;

customer and institutional development;

implementation collaboration;

strategic market development; and

the development of long-term enterprise value associated with the relationship.

The Parties intend this Warrant to arise from their strategic commercial relationship rather than from an investment of capital by the Holder into the Company.

However, neither this Warrant nor the Side Letter shall be interpreted as conclusively determining the treatment of this issuance under:

applicable securities laws;

existing financing agreements;

investor-rights agreements;

preemptive rights;

rights of first offer;

most-favored-nation provisions;

conversion provisions; or

other contractual rights applicable to the Company’s securities.

The Company shall obtain such corporate approvals, legal advice, consents, exemptions, notices, and filings as are required before issuance or exercise.

Nothing in this Warrant overrides any binding contractual right or applicable law.

4. EXERCISE PRICE

The exercise price per Warrant Share shall be:

$________________ per common share. Aggregate cash exercise cost for all 200,000 Warrant Shares: $________________ (200,000 multiplied by the approved per-share price, subject to Section 17 adjustments). Both amounts must be completed and approved before this Warrant becomes effective. No cash purchase price applies to the separate Share Award.

(the “Exercise Price”).

The Exercise Price shall be determined and approved by the Company’s Board of Directors or other authorized corporate body in consultation with counsel and in accordance with applicable corporate and securities laws.

The Parties acknowledge that the Exercise Price may be based upon fair market value, the most recent applicable financing price, another board-supported valuation methodology, or another lawful basis approved by Company counsel.

5. VESTING

5.1 Vesting Schedule

Subject to the conditions set forth below:

twenty-five percent (25%), equal to 50,000 Warrant Shares, shall vest and become exercisable on September 11, 2027, the first anniversary of the Vesting Commencement Date; and

the remaining seventy-five percent (75%), equal to 150,000 Warrant Shares, shall vest and become exercisable monthly during months thirteen (13) through forty-eight (48), ending September 11, 2030, subject to whole-share rounding below.

For each 200,000-share component separately, no shares vest before September 11, 2027; 50,000 vest on that date. On each monthly anniversary thereafter through September 11, 2030, the cumulative vested total is 50,000 plus the whole number obtained by rounding down 150,000 multiplied by the number of completed monthly installments after the cliff divided by 36. Each installment equals the increase in that cumulative total. The final installment vests the entire remaining balance so that the cumulative total is exactly 200,000 shares. Except for express acceleration, no partial month is credited. Proportionate stock-split and similar adjustments apply consistently to the totals and installments. Vesting makes purchase rights exercisable; it does not issue shares. No early exercise of unvested rights is permitted. Vested rights may be exercised at any time before this Warrant expires or otherwise terminates under its express provisions.

The “Vesting Commencement Date” shall be September 11, 2026.

5.2 Conditions to Continued Vesting

Continued vesting is conditioned upon:

the Partnership Agreement remaining in effect;

the Holder not being in an uncured material breach of the Partnership Agreement, Side Letter, or this Warrant;

the Holder continuing to materially participate in the strategic relationship in good faith; and

the Holder not having committed an Uncurable Strategic Breach.

A temporary cure period relating to an alleged curable breach shall not automatically stop vesting unless the breach remains uncured after expiration of the applicable contractual cure period.

6. TERMINATION OF PARTNERSHIP

6.1 Termination Without Holder Breach

If the Partnership Agreement expires, is not renewed, or is terminated pursuant to an applicable contractual termination right without an uncured material breach by the Holder:

all Warrant Shares vested through the effective termination date shall remain vested and exercisable subject to this Warrant; and

all then-unvested Warrant Shares shall automatically terminate as of the effective termination date.

6.2 Termination Following Holder Material Breach

If the Partnership Agreement is terminated because of the Holder’s uncured material breach:

vesting shall cease as of the effective termination date; and

all then-unvested Warrant Shares shall automatically terminate.

Any treatment of vested Warrant Shares shall be governed by this Warrant, the Side Letter, and applicable law.

6.3 Uncurable Strategic Breach

For purposes of this Warrant, “Uncurable Strategic Breach” has the meaning given in the Side Letter and includes applicable intentional misconduct such as:

intentional and material misuse of the Company’s data;

intentional unauthorized access to restricted proprietary or Confidential Information;

verified intentional circumvention of a specifically documented Shared Account opportunity or scope, as defined in the Partnership Agreement;

fraud;

willful theft or misappropriation of Company Intellectual Property;

willful misconduct causing material harm to the Company; or

comparable intentional conduct expressly designated as uncurable under the Partnership Agreement or Side Letter.

Upon an Uncurable Strategic Breach:

all unvested Warrant Shares shall immediately terminate; and

treatment of vested Warrant Shares or securities previously issued upon exercise shall be governed by this Warrant and applicable law.

Nothing in this Section creates an automatic forfeiture of vested securities unless such forfeiture is expressly enforceable under the definitive documentation and applicable law.

7. CHANGE OF CONTROL

7.1 Initial Acceleration

